1
00:00:01,620 --> 00:00:08,920
Clock, time

2
00:00:11,820 --> 00:00:17,020
Observe the clock face:

3
00:00:18,380 --> 00:00:25,160
On the clock face are numbers from 1 to 12.

4
00:00:27,050 --> 00:00:34,530
On the clock face there are also the long hand and short hand.

5
00:00:36,810 --> 00:00:45,130
When the clock shows the exact hour, the long hand always points to number 12.

6
00:00:46,730 --> 00:00:53,340
The short hand points to the corresponding hour number.

7
00:00:54,340 --> 00:00:57,900
For example:

8
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:07,160
The long hand points to number 12, the short hand points to number 3.

9
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:13,380
The clock shows 3 o'clock.

10
00:01:16,770 --> 00:01:28,980
The clock shows 9 o'clock because the short hand points to number 9, the long hand points to number 12.

